-<h1>MORDERN MAGIC GROUP LIMITED — Privacy Policy</h1>
-<p>
-<strong>Effective Date:</strong> July 20, 2026
-<br>
-<strong>Last Updated:</strong> July 20, 2026
-</p>
-<hr>
-<h2 id="sec-0">1. Introduction & Data Controller</h2>
-<p>
-MORDERN MAGIC GROUP LIMITED (MORDERN MAGIC, we, us, or our) is a company incorporated in Wyoming, United States, with its registered office at [Registered Address]. For the purposes of applicable data protection law, MORDERN MAGIC GROUP LIMITED is the data controller of your personal information collected through the Service.
-</p>
-<p>
-We are committed to protecting your privacy. This Privacy Policy explains what information we collect, how we use it, with whom we share it, and what rights you have in relation to your information. By using the Service, you acknowledge that you have read and understood this Privacy Policy.
-</p>
-<p>
-If you have any questions or wish to exercise your rights, please contact our Data Protection Officer at privacy@mordernmagic.com.
-</p>
-<hr>
-<h2 id="sec-1">2. Information We Collect</h2>
-<p>
-We collect the following categories of information:
-</p>
-<h3>2.1 Account Information</h3>
-<ul>
-  <li>Username, display name, email address</li>
-  <li>Password (stored as a one-way hash, not in plaintext)</li>
-  <li>Profile photo (optional, user-provided)</li>
-  <li>Date of birth (for age verification)</li>
-  <li>Country/region (for content availability and tax calculation)</li>
-</ul>
-<h3>2.3 Third-Party Login Information</h3>
-<p>
-If you sign in via a third-party identity provider, we receive:
-</p>
-<ul>
-  <li>TikTok: open_id, union_id, nickname, avatar</li>
-  <li>Google: Google account ID, email, profile photo</li>
-  <li>Apple: Apple User ID, email (may be a private relay)</li>
-  <li>Facebook: Facebook User ID, name, email</li>
-</ul>
-<h3>2.3 Order and Payment Information</h3>
-<ul>
-  <li>Transaction history (subscription, virtual currency, pay-per-episode)</li>
-  <li>Payment method type (e.g., Visa, Mastercard, PayPal — not the full card number)</li>
-  <li>Billing receipts and invoices</li>
-  <li>All actual payment processing is performed by TikTok Pay. We do not collect or store your full payment card number.</li>
-</ul>
-<h3>2.4 Device and Technical Information</h3>
-<ul>
-  <li>IP address</li>
-  <li>Device type, manufacturer, model</li>
-  <li>Operating system and version</li>
-  <li>Unique device identifiers (IDFA, GAID, OAID)</li>
-  <li>Browser type and version (for web access)</li>
-  <li>Mobile carrier information</li>
-  <li>Time zone setting and language preference</li>
-  <li>App version</li>
-</ul>
-<h3>2.5 Usage and Behavioral Information</h3>
-<ul>
-  <li>Content viewing history (titles, episodes watched, completion rate)</li>
-  <li>Search queries within the Service</li>
-  <li>Liked, favorited, and bookmarked content</li>
-  <li>Comments and reviews submitted</li>
-  <li>Time spent on the Service</li>
-</ul>
-<h3>2.6 Cookies and Tracking Technologies (Web)</h3>
-<ul>
-  <li>Essential cookies (session, authentication, security)</li>
-  <li>Analytics cookies (page views, performance)</li>
-  <li>Marketing cookies (with your consent)</li>
-  <li>We use cookies and similar tracking technologies in accordance with applicable law, including the EU ePrivacy Directive.</li>
-</ul>
-<h3>2.7 Push Notification Token</h3>
-<ul>
-  <li>Device push token (for sending notifications you have opted in to)</li>
-  <li>Notification interaction history (delivery, open, dismiss)</li>
-</ul>
-<h3>2.8 User-Generated Content</h3>
-<ul>
-  <li>Reviews, comments, ratings</li>
-  <li>Customer support inquiries</li>
-  <li>Survey responses</li>
-</ul>
-<hr>
-<h2 id="sec-2">3. How We Use Your Information</h2>
-<p>
-We use your information for the following purposes:
-</p>
-<ol>
-  <li>To provide and operate the Service, including processing transactions and delivering content.</li>
-  <li>To manage your account, including authentication, authorization, and customer support.</li>
-  <li>To personalize your experience, including content recommendations based on viewing history and preferences.</li>
-  <li>To communicate with you, including transactional notifications, service updates, security alerts, and (with your consent) marketing communications.</li>
-  <li>To detect, prevent, and address fraud, abuse, security issues, and violations of our Terms.</li>
-  <li>To comply with legal obligations, including tax, accounting, anti-money laundering, and law enforcement requests.</li>
-  <li>To enforce our Terms and protect our rights, property, and safety, and that of our users and third parties.</li>
-  <li>To improve the Service, including analytics, research, and product development.</li>
-  <li>To process payments and prevent fraudulent transactions, in coordination with TikTok Pay and payment processors.</li>
-</ol>
-<p>
-We do not use your content viewing history for purposes that are incompatible with those listed above.
-</p>
-<hr>
-<h2 id="sec-3">4. Legal Basis for Processing (GDPR)</h2>
-<p>
-If you are in the European Economic Area, United Kingdom, or Switzerland, we process your personal information on the following legal bases under the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR):
-</p>
-<ul>
-  <li>Contract (Article 6(1)(b)): To provide the Service you have requested, including subscription management and content delivery.</li>
-  <li>Legitimate Interests (Article 6(1)(f)): To operate, secure, and improve the Service, prevent fraud, and enforce our Terms, where our interests are not overridden by your fundamental rights.</li>
-  <li>Consent (Article 6(1)(a)): For non-essential cookies, marketing communications, and certain analytics. You may withdraw your consent at any time.</li>
-  <li>Legal Obligation (Article 6(1)(c)): To comply with applicable laws, regulations, and legal processes.</li>
-  <li>Vital Interests (Article 6(1)(d)): To protect your vital interests or those of another person in exceptional circumstances.</li>
-</ul>
-<hr>
-<h2 id="sec-4">5. How We Share Your Information</h2>
-<p>
-We do not sell your personal information. We share your information only as follows:
-</p>
-<h3>5.1 Service Providers</h3>
-<p>
-We share information with third-party service providers that perform services on our behalf, including:
-</p>
-<ul>
-  <li>Cloud hosting and storage (e.g., AWS, Google Cloud, Aliyun)</li>
-  <li>Content delivery network (CDN) providers</li>
-  <li>Customer support platforms</li>
-  <li>Email and notification delivery (e.g., OneSignal, PushEngage, SendGrid)</li>
-  <li>Analytics providers (e.g., Google Analytics, Firebase, AppsFlyer, Adjust)</li>
-  <li>Payment processors (primarily TikTok Pay)</li>
-  <li>Customer data platform (e.g., Segment, mParticle)</li>
-  <li>Marketing and advertising partners (only with your consent where required)</li>
-</ul>
-<h3>5.2 Advertising and Attribution Partners</h3>
-<p>
-With your consent (where required), we share information with:
-</p>
-<ul>
-  <li>TikTok Pixel and TikTok Events API (for ad attribution and optimization)</li>
-  <li>Facebook Pixel and Conversions API</li>
-  <li>Google Ads and Google Marketing Platform</li>
-  <li>Apple Search Ads</li>
-  <li>AppsFlyer, Adjust, Branch (mobile attribution)</li>
-</ul>
-<h3>5.3 TikTok and Other Platforms</h3>
-<ul>
-  <li>As a TikTok mini program, we receive certain information from TikTok and share certain information with TikTok, subject to TikTok's Privacy Policy and our data sharing arrangements.</li>
-  <li>If you sign in via TikTok, Google, Apple, or Facebook, those platforms receive notice of your sign-in.</li>
-</ul>
-<h3>5.4 Legal Requirements</h3>
-<p>
-We may disclose your information:
-</p>
-<ul>
-  <li>To comply with applicable law, regulation, court order, or legal process.</li>
-  <li>To respond to lawful requests from public authorities, including law enforcement.</li>
-  <li>To protect our rights, property, or safety, or that of our users or third parties.</li>
-  <li>To detect, prevent, or address fraud, security, or technical issues.</li>
-  <li>In connection with a corporate transaction (merger, acquisition, financing, restructuring, or sale of assets), with appropriate confidentiality protections.</li>
-</ul>
-<h3>5.5 Aggregate or De-identified Information</h3>
-<p>
-We may share aggregate or de-identified information with third parties for research, analytics, marketing, or other purposes, provided that such information cannot reasonably be used to identify you.
-</p>
-<hr>
-<h2 id="sec-5">6. International Data Transfers</h2>
-<p>
-Your information may be transferred to and processed in countries other than your country of residence, including the United States, China, Singapore, and other countries where our service providers operate.
-</p>
-<p>
-For transfers from the European Economic Area, United Kingdom, or Switzerland to countries not deemed adequate by the European Commission, we rely on appropriate safeguards, including:
-</p>
-<ul>
-  <li>Standard Contractual Clauses (SCC) approved by the European Commission</li>
-  <li>The UK International Data Transfer Addendum (where applicable)</li>
-  <li>Binding Corporate Rules (where applicable)</li>
-  <li>Your explicit consent (where applicable)</li>
-</ul>
-<p>
-For transfers from other jurisdictions, we comply with applicable local data localization requirements.
-</p>
-<p>
-You may contact privacy@mordernmagic.com to request a copy of the transfer safeguards applicable to your data.
-</p>
-<hr>
-<h2 id="sec-6">7. Data Retention</h2>
-<p>
-We retain your personal information for as long as necessary to provide the Service and fulfill the purposes described in this Policy, unless a longer retention period is required or permitted by law.
-</p>
-<p>
-Specific retention periods include:
-</p>
-<ul>
-  <li>Account information: For the duration of your account, plus 30 days after deletion to allow for recovery.</li>
-  <li>Transaction records: 7 years (for tax and accounting purposes).</li>
-  <li>Viewing history: 24 months.</li>
-  <li>Marketing consent records: Until you withdraw consent, plus 3 years.</li>
-  <li>Support correspondence: 3 years.</li>
-  <li>Server logs: 90 days.</li>
-  <li>Backup data: Up to 12 months in encrypted form.</li>
-</ul>
-<p>
-When personal information is no longer needed, we securely delete or anonymize it.
-</p>
-<hr>
-<h2 id="sec-7">8. Your Rights by Region</h2>
-<p>
-Depending on your jurisdiction, you have the following rights:
-</p>
-<h3>8.1 European Economic Area, United Kingdom, and Switzerland (GDPR/UK GDPR)</h3>
-<ul>
